 "not_certified_here": "The LightGBM / internal/experiment shadow ranker (not live in simple mode). The Wilson trending gate and the HLL window edge (first slice, still unverified). Watch-history controls (A12). Suggestion bans and autosuggest thresholds (A13 first slice).",
 "findings_recorded_not_fixed": [
  "FIXED in user#165, recorded because it was live: both discovery rails fetched before the session settled on a hard load; the watch page's related rail thereby bypassed the viewer's own mute/block filter.",
  "Co-visitation has no k-anonymity floor: one user's single session publishes a public neighbour edge, while autosuggest and trending both enforce minimum_query_user_count=3.",
  "In the shipped search_mode=simple default, co-visitation reaches no product surface at all: relatedSimple/homeSimple never read item_neighbors.",
  "total can undercount the page it ships (core's SQL recall vs vidra-search's trigram recall) \u2014 cross-repo contract decision.",
  "Clear-all does not reach the Redis session-recency list (sess:q:<session-id>, TTL ~2h), so cleared queries keep coming back as personal suggestions under copy promising permanence.",
  "reason='subscribed' is reported for channels the viewer never subscribed to (channel-affinity relabel at 0.8; vidra-search holds no subscription data).",
  "SearchSettingsView gates the personalized-SEARCH toggle on simple mode with an honest reason but leaves the personalized-RECOMMENDATIONS toggle ungated, although it is equally inert in simple mode."
 ],
 "src03_remaining_gap": "Only the clause 'no personalized data when off'. Opting out stops SERVING completely (zero user_search_history rows, zero user_watch_projection rows, no personal suggestions, an item-for-item anonymous home rail, personalized=false on the wire) but not COLLECTION: an opted-out user's searches still land in query_log and behavior_events under their raw account UUID with their raw query text, still count toward the instance-wide k-anonymity floor, their plays still bump trending under a Redis guard key named with their account UUID, and their queries are written to the ~2 h sess:q:<session-id> Redis list (not served back to them \u2014 the read side is gated). The shipped UI copy only promises that new searches are not stored to YOUR HISTORY. Owner ruling pending. If the ruling is that the shipped copy is the promise, SRC-03 can flip on this evidence plus the first slice's, and the row's phrase 'user search-discovery opt-in' should be corrected to opt-OUT."
}